      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">25 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Heap / top-k</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Bucket sort</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/top-k-frequent-elements/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 347</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Top K Frequent Elements</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">A count can never be bigger than n, so use the count itself as an array index: count with a hash map, drop each value into <code>bucket[count]</code>, and read buckets from the top until you have k values. O(n) time, O(n) space; the size-k min-heap (O(n log k)) is the version most interviewers expect you to say first.</p>\n"
  },
